    "markdown": "![ACL Logo](https://aclanthology.org/images/acl-logo.svg) ACL Anthology ⟨1⟩\n  * About⟨2⟩\n    * Announcements⟨3⟩\n    * Communication channels⟨4⟩\n    * Related work⟨5⟩\n    * Copyright⟨6⟩\n    * * * *\n    * Credits⟨7⟩\n    * Volunteer⟨8⟩\n    * Development⟨9⟩\n    * Feedback⟨10⟩\n  * Using⟨2⟩\n    * Citing papers⟨11⟩\n    * Links in the Anthology⟨12⟩\n    * Data access⟨13⟩\n    * * * *\n    * All FAQs⟨14⟩\n    * * * *\n    * ###### Details\n    * Anthology identifiers⟨15⟩\n    * Names⟨16⟩\n    * ORCID iDs⟨17⟩\n    * DOIs⟨18⟩\n    * Verified authors⟨19⟩\n  * Contributions⟨2⟩\n    * Submissions⟨20⟩\n    * Corrections⟨21⟩\n    * Author pages⟨22⟩\n    * Attachments⟨23⟩\n  * GitHub⟨24⟩\n\n\n## Proceedings of Machine Translation Summit XI: Tutorials\nBente Maegaard⟨25⟩ (Editor)\n* * * \n\nAnthology ID:\n    2007.mtsummit-tutorials \n\nMonth:\n    September 10 \n\nYear:\n    2007 \n\nAddress:\n    Copenhagen, Denmark \n\nVenue:\n    MTSummit⟨26⟩ \n\nEvent:\n    Machine Translation Summit (2007)⟨27⟩ \n\nSIG:\n\n\nPublisher:\n\n\nURL:\n    <https://aclanthology.org/2007.mtsummit-tutorials/> \n\nDOI:\n\n\nBib Export formats:\n     BibTeX⟨28⟩ MODS XML⟨29⟩ EndNote⟨30⟩\nBibTeX ⟨28⟩Search⟨31⟩\n* * *\npdf ⟨32⟩bib ⟨33⟩⟨34⟩\n**Statistical machine translation⟨35⟩**  \nKevin Knight⟨36⟩ | Philipp Koehn⟨37⟩\npdf ⟨38⟩bib ⟨39⟩⟨40⟩\n**Example based machine translation for cross-lingual information retrieval⟨41⟩**  \nCristina Vertan⟨42⟩\npdf ⟨43⟩bib ⟨44⟩⟨45⟩\n**Context-based evaluation of MT systems: principles and tools⟨46⟩**  \nMaghi King⟨47⟩ | Andrei Popescu-Belis⟨48⟩ | Paula Estrella⟨49⟩\npdf ⟨50⟩bib ⟨51⟩\n**Using free online MT in multilingual websites⟨52⟩**  \nFederico Gaspari⟨53⟩ | Harold Somers⟨54⟩\npdf ⟨55⟩bib ⟨56⟩\n**LTC tutorial on workflow and business information management in the language industry⟨57⟩**  \nAdriane Rinsche⟨58⟩\npdf ⟨59⟩bib ⟨60⟩\n**How to successfully integrate MT⟨61⟩**  \nJen Doyon⟨62⟩\n![Creative Commons License](https://i.creativecommons.org/l/by/4.0/88x31.png)⟨63⟩ ACL materials are Copyright © 1963–2026 ACL; other materials are copyrighted by their respective copyright holders. Materials prior to 2016 here are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 International License⟨64⟩. Permission is granted to make copies for the purposes of teaching and research. Materials published in or after 2016 are licensed on a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License⟨65⟩.\nThe ACL Anthology is managed and built by the ACL Anthology team⟨7⟩ of volunteers.\n_Site last built on 22 July 2026 at 14:46 UTC withcommit 280e4ed⟨66⟩._\n",
